      "value": "i think this would be a good change to add some nuance to the very poor range, but i also think we shouldn't do away completely with value judegements. Second Life uses this complexity system and well, performance is kind of a runaway problem there. I think color-coding the complexity number to line up with the excellent-good-medium-poor-very poor metrics would be a good compromise.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
